ld/bazel/issues/7165#issuecomment-460993080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/7165","id":460993080,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDk5MzA4MA==","user":{"login":"dslomov","id":5008223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDgyMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5008223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov","html_url":"https://github.com/dslomov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-06T11:38:12Z","updated_at":"2019-02-06T11:38:12Z","body":"> If a novice user uses rules_typescript, but didn't install the typescript dependency via npm, then they get this error:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ERROR: C:/users/alexeagle/projects/try_bazel/BUILD.bazel:3:1: every rule of type ts_library implicitly depends upon the target '@npm//typescript:typescript__typings', but this target could not be found because of: no such package '@npm//typescript': BUILD file not found on package path\r\n> ERROR: Analysis of target '//:root' failed; build aborted: no such package '@npm//typescript': BUILD file not found on package path\r\n> ```\r\n> Bazel knows that the ts_library rule has an attribute that refers to `@npm//typescript:typescript__typings`. It could print the docstring from that attribute, or allow the ts_library rule some other way to help the user fix the error.\r\n\r\nI guess we could add smth like `error_doc` argument to attr.label that will be a way to provide a message for implicit attributes that cannot be resolved.\r\n\r\n> Another way to fix this would be for rules_nodejs to be able to intercept all `no such package: @npm//...` messages and say \"you need to npm install this package\"\r\n\r\nThis probably requires much more design...\r\nAnother way to solve this for Angular would be for the angular cli to intercept this message and provide some suggestion in npm terms - wdyt @alexeagle?\r\n\r\n@aehlig wdyt in general?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/460993080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"dslomov","id":5008223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDgyMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5008223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov","html_url":"https://github.com/dslomov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2120986480,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MjEyMDk4NjQ4MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/2120986480","actor":{"login":"alexeagle","id":47395,"node_id":"MDQ6